wiki/docs/logistics_networks.mdx:18:- Items: with seeds that have no traits it puts out about 24 items a second. With seeds maxed in Productive Farming's Growth and Yield it puts out about 320 items a second, which is more than a gold upgrade moves.
wiki/docs/logistics_networks.mdx:19:- Upgrade needed: a diamond upgrade covers up to 7 such planter blocks, and power is the limit. More than 7 needs a netherite upgrade, or more nodes on the power blocks.
wiki/docs/cloche.mdx:5:The core applies a cloche to every planter block. It always works and needs no item. It uses ATE's configured cloche speed and yield bonuses.
wiki/docs/cloche.mdx:7:ATE rounds a 1-item drop at 1.1 yield back to 1, so a cloche does nothing for Mystical Agriculture essence there. The built-in cloche keeps the fraction that rounding throws away and gives one extra item each time it adds up to 1. With the default numbers that is one extra item every tenth harvest.
wiki/docs/growing.mdx:8:- Growth time, power and fertilizer follow ATE's formulas and are read from ATE's live config. Power is drawn each tick for every seed that is still growing. If the power blocks can't cover a planter block's full draw, its seeds stop growing for that tick. Seeds that are already ready still harvest.
wiki/docs/ae2.mdx:11:- Every `me_interval` ticks the ME block moves the export blocks' contents into ME and tops the fertilizer blocks up from ME with the fertilizer set in its filter slot.
wiki/docs/ae2.mdx:23:A Flux Accessor placed against the core or a power block also charges it, with or without an ME block.
